From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:12:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] Add Gemini 3.8 Flash high rolling-summary profiles

Two profiles between google-gemini-3-8-flash-high (Standard) and
google-gemini-3-8-flash-high-provider-adapter, so the path changes one
harness setting at a time:

- google-gemini-3-8-flash-high-rolling-summary: the Standard profile
  (manual_rolling on the Interactions API, visible text only, carry-forward
  instruction on) with the Provider Adapter's harness_summary compaction
  (175k provider-token trigger, 8,192-token summary cap, 8,192 headroom)
  and its MAX_CONTEXT_LENGTH of 1,048,576, so oldest-turn trimming does not
  fire before the summary trigger.
- google-gemini-3-8-flash-high-rolling-summary-notes-off: the same profile
  with agent.carry_forward_instruction=false; its system prompt equals the
  Provider Adapter's.

Client, request and pricing blocks are identical to both ends of the path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
